- 'show me all customer accounts' / 'get all customer accounts' / 'list all customers' / 'list customer accounts' / 'show me recent customer accounts' -> target_entity 'CustomerAccount' with NO filters and NO include. This is a plain-list request about the customer-account collection as a whole. Do NOT require a customer name or account number here; the collection is the answer, and a bounded sample is returned with the honest total. IMPORTANT: an account-balance question ("account balance for customer X") and a customer-invoices question ("AR invoices for customer X") name a specific customer and route to the resolver path — those are NOT this shape. This rule fires ONLY when the request names no customer and no account number: a bare 'show me all customer accounts' or a paraphrase with a list-shaped verb but no identifier.
- 'show me all customer accounts balance' / 'customer accounts balance' — where 'balance' is an adjective on the collection with no customer named — this is NOT a filter-less list. The balance-only shape requires a customer name to identify which account's balance is asked for; refuse with a missing_identifier refusal naming that requirement. Do NOT route this to the CustomerAccount list above just because the words 'customer accounts' appear.
